nghệ Kỹ thuật Môi trường  aIncludes bibliographies and indexes.  aWater chemistry.  aJenkins, David00668nam a2200229 a 45000010006000000050011000060200015000170200018000320400011000500410008000610820015000690900017000841000021001012450076001222500012001982600045002103000032002555000068002876500019003556500047003747000017004215369628/01/2021  a157766678X  a9781577666783  aDHSPKT  aEng  a628.53223  a628.53bC776  aCooper, C. David  aAir pollution control:ba design approach/cC. David Cooper, F.C. Alley  a4th ed.  aLong Grove, Ill.:bWaveland Press,c2011  axvi, 839 p.:bill.;c23 cm.  aSử dụng cho ngành Công nghệ Kỹ thuật môi trường  aAirxPollution  aAirxPurificationxEquipment and supplies.  aAlley, F. C.01730nam a2200289 a 45000010006000000050011000060200018000170400011000350410008000460820012000540900014000661000023000802450060001032500012001632600036001753000033002115000068002445040041003125200932003536500026012856500021013116500022013326500019013546500019013736500028013926500020014205369528/01/2021  a9781489977151  aDHSPKT  aEng  a660223  a660bL657  aLevenspiel, Octave  aEngineering flow and heat exchange/cOctave Levenspiel.  a3rd ed.  aNew York, NY:bSpringer,c2014.  axxiv, 398 p.:bill.;c24 cm.  aSử dụng cho ngành Công nghệ Kỹ thuật Môi trường  aIncludes bibliographies and indexes.  aThe third edition of Engineering Flow and Heat Exchange is the most practical textbook available on the design of heat transfer and equipment. This book is an excellent introduction to real-world applications for advanced undergraduates and an indispensable reference for professionals. The book includes comprehensive chapters on the different types and classifications of fluids, how to analyze fluids, and where a particular fluid fits into a broader picture. This book includes various a wide variety of problems and solutions - some whimsical and others directly from industrial applications. Numerous practical examples of heat transfer Different from other introductory books on fluids Clearly written, simple to understand, written for students to absorb material quickly Discusses non-Newtonian as well as Newtonian fluids Covers the entire field concisely Solutions manual with worked examples and solutions provided.  aChemical engineering.  aFluid mechanics.  aHeat engineering.  aHeat transfer.  aMass transfer.  aMechanical engineering.  aThermodynamics.00756nam a2200229 a 45000010006000000050011000060200018000170400011000350410008000460820015000540900016000691000029000852450083001142600038001973000033002355000068002685040041003366500032003776500029004096500042004386500046004805369728/01/2021  a9781138035201  aDHSPKT  aEng  a628.44223  a628.44bK14  aKalogirou, Efstratios N.  aWaste-to-energy technologies and global applications/cEfstratios N. Kalogirou  aBoca Raton, FL:bCRC Press,c2018  axxii, 243 p.:bill.;c24 cm.  aSử dụng cho ngành Công nghệ Kỹ thuật môi trường  aIncludes bibliographical references.  aRefuse and refuse disposal.  aSustainable engineering.  aWaste products as fuelvCase studies.  aWaste products as fuelxEconomic aspects.01278nam a2200229 a 45000010006000000050011000060200018000170400011000350410008000460820015000540900017000691000017000862450036001032600037001393000047001765000068002235040051002915200605003426500020009476500053009676500028010205369828/01/2021  a9780081010426  aDHSPKT  aEng  a662.87223  a662.87bB832  aBreeze, Paul  aEnergy from waste/cPaul Breeze  aLondon:bAcademic Press,c[2018]  avi, 91 pages:billustrations, map;c23 cm.  aSử dụng cho ngành Công nghệ Kỹ thuật môi trường  aIncludes bibliographical references and index.  aEnergy from Waste is a concise, up-to-date and accessible guide on how to create power from both urban and industrial waste. The book explores the types of waste that, instead of going to landfill, can be converted to energy, also discussing the most up-to-date technologies for doing so. The book contains a strong emphasis on the related environmental impacts and economic factors involved in the various methods of generating electricity, making this a valuable and insightful read for those involved in the management and conversion of waste, including energy engineers, managers and technicians.  aRefuse as fuel.  aTECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERINGxChemical & Biochemical  aWaste products as fuel.01539nam a2200289 a 45000010006000000050011000060200018000170400011000350410008000460820019000540900021000731000023000942450100001172500020002172600037002373000044002745000068003185040051003865200628004376500034010656500016010996500020011156500027011356500034011626500031011967000022012275369928/01/2021  a9781260441604  aDHSPKT  aEng  a613.101579223  a613.101579bR615  aRittmann, Bruce E.  aEnvironmental biotechnology:bprinciples and applications/cBruce E. Rittmann, Perry L. McCarty  aSecond edition.  aNew York :bMcGraw-Hill,c[2020]  axvii, 633 pages:billustrations;c25 cm  aSử dụng cho ngành Công nghệ Kỹ thuật môi trường  aIncludes bibliographical references and index.  a"This thoroughly revised educational resource presents the biological principles that underlie modern microbiological treatment technologies. Written by two of the field's foremost researchers, Environmental Biotechnology: Principles and Applications, Second Edition clearly explains the new technologies that have evolved over the past twenty years, including direct anaerobic treatments, membrane-based processes, and granular processes. The first half of the book focuses on theory and tools; the second half offers practical applications that are clearly illustrated through real-world examples"cProvided by publisher.  aBiodegradation, Environmental  aBioreactors  aBioremediation.  aBiotechnologyxmethods  aEnvironmental Healthxmethods  aEnvironmental Microbiology  aMcCarty, Perry L.00